    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d707">

                <pb facs="0625" n="549" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg549"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/18176</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Special Agent Silliman
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-05-18">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 18, 1916</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your May 15, 4 p.m. It is assumed <hi rendition="#italic">de facto</hi>
                    Government will not oppose pursuit of bandits raiding American territory while
                    matters discussed at Scott-Obregon conference are subject of negotiations
                    between both Governments. If you think Governor apt to carry out threat to
                    oppose pursuit bandits, discreetly call above to his attention.</p>
                <p>American force pursuing Glen Springs raiders into Mexican territory.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
